cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the audit protocol, please cite the paper below."
title: "Resampling Buys What the Classifier Cannot Carve Out: Minority-Class Detection on CIC-IDS2017 under a Purged Temporal Split"
abstract: >-
  A 70/30 flow-level split of CIC-IDS2017 leaks at capture-session level:
  99.75% of benign test flows have a same-class training flow within ten rows
  of the same capture file. Re-cutting each (session, class) group into
  contiguous 60/15/25% blocks with a boundary purge removes the leak, and
  holding groups and cut points fixed while shuffling only the order isolates
  its cost at 0.083 macro-F1 and 0.614 lesion-group F1 sum. The loss is one
  class: Bot falls from 0.605 to 0.000 while Brute Force and XSS stay flat.
  Resampling is not a leakage artifact; what it is worth is a property of the
  classifier, not of the features.
